  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "A tunning fork of frequency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>340</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math> resonates in the fundamental mode with an air column of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>125</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> in a cylindrical tube closed at one end. When water is slowly poured in it, the minimum height of water required for observing resonance once again is _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cm</mi></math>.<br />(Velocity of sound in air is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>340</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ms</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "50",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>We know that,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>f</mi></math>, then,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>v</mi><mi>f</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>340</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>340</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>340</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>340</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></p><p>First resonating length,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>100</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math></p><p>Second resonating length,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>75</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math></p><p>Third&nbsp;resonating length,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>125</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math></p><p>So third resonance is not possible since the length of the tube is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>125</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math></p><p>Thus, minimum height of water necessary for resonance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>125</mn><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>75</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/b50d34b3-6d9f-458c-a072-38fa0d1e087e-image.png\" style=\"width: 220px; height: 153px;\" /></p>",
